## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical cost-benefit analysis thinking for privacy-conscious mobile features with offline-first architecture. It tests understanding of storage trade-offs, energy budgeting, consent management, and long-term maintenance considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first storage and local geofence processing to ensure reliability without network connectivity
- Energy budgeting for continuous location monitoring and CPU usage for geofence checks
- Privacy, consent, and data minimization requirements for location-based features
- Cloud synchronization trade-offs for shared calendar data and conflict resolution
- Rollout planning with phased deployment and offline fallback behavior
- Technical debt and drift/maintenance costs over the feature lifecycle

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: register geofence, trigger locally, and schedule reminder
registerGeofence(reminder.id, reminder.coordinates, reminder.radius, async (trigger) => {
  const localReminder = await db.getReminder(reminder.id);
  if (localReminder) {
    await notificationManager.show(localReminder);
    await syncQueue.add({ reminderId: reminder.id, triggeredAt: Date.now() });
  }
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device crypto trade-offs for privacy-focused apps.

## Key Concepts
- On-device key management
- Key rotation cadence
- AES-256-GCM encryption
- Impact on battery, CPU, memory
- Privacy/compliance costs

## Code Example
```javascript
async function encryptNote(note, key) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const alg = { name: 'AES-GCM', iv };
  const ciphertext = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(alg, key, enc.encode(note));
  return { iv, ciphertext: new Uint8Array(ciphertext) };
}
```

